{
  "about": "Colour strings and whether Chrome takes them, as the pixel each paints. Read by tests/css_grammar.rs for `Context2D::set_fill_style_css` and by tests/suite/css-grammar.test.js for `ctx.fillStyle`, so the two surfaces answer one table. Comments, `currentcolor` and whitespace: the colour functions' own grammar is pinned in tests/native_api_contract.rs.",
  "source": "Chrome 152.0.7977.167: ctx.fillStyle set to `#010203` on a fresh 2D context of a canvas outside a document, then to the string, a pixel filled and read back with getImageData, measured 2026-10-26. A refused row is one Chrome ignored, leaving `#010203`; `rgba` is the 8-bit pixel of each it took.",
  "knownDifferences": "Left out: a comment beside a keyword. Chrome 152 ignores `red/**/`, `/**/red`, `red /**/`, `transparent/**/`, `currentcolor/**/` and `red/*`, and takes a comment beside a hex colour or a function. CSS Syntax drops a comment when it tokenizes, so each of those is a valid <color>, and here each is read; docs/browser-differences.md says so.",
